{"page_content": "ACME/Flame Design Final Report (2023) \n \n6 April 2023 \n72 \n \n \nFigure 1 shows the inverse spherical flame growing with time to reach enough fuel to consume the oxygen \nflowing from the porous spherical burner. As the flame grew bigger, the radiative heat loss increased, \nwhich caused the flame to weaken and become dimmer. The flame's temperature dropped, which is \nindicated by the hue of the glowing ceramic fibers, where yellow is hotter than orange, which in turn is \nhotter than red.", "metadata": {"source": "PSI-10_Reports_FinalRpt_ACMEFlameDesign.pdf", "page": 72}}